#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.46 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:5
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:9
msgid ""
"The \"--rfc\" option of \"git format-patch\" learned to take an optional "
"string value to be used in place of \"RFC\" to tweak the \"[PATCH]\" on the "
"subject header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:13
msgid ""
"The credential helper protocol, together with the HTTP layer, have been "
"enhanced to support authentication schemes different from username & "
"password pair, like Bearer and NTLM."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:17
msgid ""
"Command line completion script (in contrib/) learned to complete \"git "
"symbolic-ref\" a bit better (you need to enable plumbing commands to be "
"completed with GIT_COMPLETION_SHOW_ALL_COMMANDS)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:22
msgid ""
"When the user responds to a prompt given by \"git add -p\" with an "
"unsupported command, list of available commands were given, which was too "
"much if the user knew what they wanted to type but merely made a typo.  Now "
"the user gets a much shorter error message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:25
msgid ""
"The color parsing code learned to handle 12-bit RGB colors, spelled as "
"\"#RGB\" (in addition to \"#RRGGBB\" that is already supported)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:29
msgid ""
"The operation mode options (like \"--get\") the \"git config\" command uses "
"have been deprecated and replaced with subcommands (like \"git config "
"get\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:32
msgid ""
"\"git tag\" learned the \"--trailer\" option to futz with the trailers in "
"the same way as \"git commit\" does."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:35
msgid ""
"A new global \"--no-advice\" option can be used to disable all advice "
"messages, which is meant to be used only in scripts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:38
msgid "Updates to symbolic refs can now be made as a part of ref transaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:40
msgid "The trailer API has been reshuffled a bit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:43
msgid "Terminology to call various ref-like things are getting straightened out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:47
msgid ""
"The command line completion script (in contrib/) has been adjusted to the "
"recent update to \"git config\" that adopted subcommand based UI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:50
msgid ""
"The knobs to tweak how reftable files are written have been made available "
"as configuration variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:56
msgid ""
"When \"git push\" notices that the commit at the tip of the ref on the other "
"side it is about to overwrite does not exist locally, it used to first try "
"fetching it if the local repository is a partial clone. The command has been "
"taught not to do so and immediately fail instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:59
msgid ""
"The promisor.quiet configuration knob can be set to true to make lazy "
"fetching from promisor remotes silent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:64
msgid ""
"The inter/range-diff output has been moved to the end of the patch when "
"format-patch adds it to a single patch, instead of writing it before the "
"patch text, to be consistent with what is done for a cover letter for a "
"multi-patch series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:68
msgid ""
"A new command has been added to migrate a repository that uses the files "
"backend for its ref storage to use the reftable backend, with limitations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:73
msgid ""
"\"git diff --exit-code --ext-diff\" learned to take the exit status of the "
"external diff driver into account when deciding the exit status of the "
"overall \"git diff\" invocation when configured to do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:76
msgid ""
"\"git update-ref --stdin\" learned to handle transactional updates of "
"symbolic-refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:80
msgid ""
"\"git format-patch --interdiff\" for multi-patch series learned to turn on "
"cover letters automatically (unless told never to enable cover letter with "
"\"--no-cover-letter\" and such)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:83
msgid ""
"The \"--heads\" option of \"ls-remote\" and \"show-ref\" has been "
"deprecated; \"--branches\" replaces \"--heads\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:87
msgid ""
"For over a year, setting add.interactive.useBuiltin configuration variable "
"did nothing but giving a \"this does not do anything\" warning.  The warning "
"has been removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:90
msgid ""
"The http transport can now be told to send request with authentication "
"material without first getting a 401 response."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:92
msgid "A handful of entries are added to the GitFAQ document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:96
msgid ""
"\"git var GIT_SHELL_PATH\" should report the path to the shell used to spawn "
"external commands, but it didn't do so on Windows, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:99
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:103
msgid ""
"Advertise \"git contacts\", a tool for newcomers to find people to ask "
"review for their patches, a bit more in our developer documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:107
msgid ""
"In addition to building the objects needed, try to link the objects that are "
"used in fuzzer tests, to make sure at least they build without bitrot, in "
"Linux CI runs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:110
msgid "Code to write out reftable has seen some optimization and simplification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:113
msgid ""
"Tests to ensure interoperability between reftable written by jgit and our "
"code have been added and enabled in CI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:117
msgid ""
"The singleton index_state instance \"the_index\" has been eliminated by "
"always instantiating \"the_repository\" and replacing references to "
"\"the_index\" with references to its .index member."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:119
msgid "Git-GUI has a new maintainer, Johannes Sixt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:122
msgid ""
"The \"test-tool\" has been taught to run testsuite tests in parallel, "
"bypassing the need to use the \"prove\" tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:125
msgid ""
"The \"whitespace check\" task that was enabled for GitHub Actions CI has "
"been ported to GitLab CI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:129
msgid ""
"The refs API lost functions that implicitly assumes to work on the primary "
"ref_store by forcing the callers to pass a ref_store as an argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:132
msgid ""
"Code clean-up to reduce inter-function communication inside builtin/config.c "
"done via the use of global variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:134
msgid "The pack bitmap code saw some clean-up to prepare for a follow-up topic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:136
msgid "Preliminary code clean-up for \"git send-email\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:139
msgid ""
"The default \"creation-factor\" used by \"git format-patch\" has been raised "
"to make it more aggressively find matching commits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:144
msgid ""
"Before discovering the repository details, We used to assume SHA-1 as the "
"\"default\" hash function, which has been corrected. Hopefully this will "
"smoke out codepaths that rely on such an unwarranted assumptions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:146
msgid "The project decision making policy has been documented."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:149
msgid "The strcmp-offset tests have been rewritten using the unit test framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:152
msgid ""
"\"git add -p\" learned to complain when an answer with more than one letter "
"is given to a prompt that expects a single letter answer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:154
msgid "The alias-expanded command lines are logged to the trace output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:157
msgid ""
"A new test was added to ensure git commands that are designed to run outside "
"repositories do work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:160
msgid ""
"A few tests in reftable library have been rewritten using the unit test "
"framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:163
msgid ""
"A pair of test helpers that essentially are unit tests on hash algorithms "
"have been rewritten using the unit-tests framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:166
msgid ""
"A test helper that essentially is unit tests on the \"decorate\" logic has "
"been rewritten using the unit-tests framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:169
msgid "Many memory leaks in the sparse-checkout code paths have been plugged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:173
msgid ""
"\"make check-docs\" noticed problems and reported to its output but failed "
"to signal its findings with its exit status, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:175
msgid "Building with \"-Werror -Wwrite-strings\" is now supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:178
msgid ""
"To help developers, the build procedure now allows builders to use "
"CFLAGS_APPEND to specify additional CFLAGS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:180
msgid "\"oidtree\" tests were rewritten to use the unit test framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:184
msgid ""
"The structure of the document that records longer-term project decisions to "
"deprecate/remove/update various behaviour has been outlined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:188
msgid ""
"The pseudo-merge reachability bitmap to help more efficient storage of the "
"reachability bitmap in a repository with too many refs has been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:193
msgid ""
"When \"git merge\" sees that the index cannot be refreshed (e.g. due to "
"another process doing the same in the background), it died but after writing "
"MERGE_HEAD etc. files, which was useless for the purpose to recover from the "
"failure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:197
msgid ""
"The output from \"git cat-file --batch-check\" and \"--batch-command "
"(info)\" should not be unbuffered, for which some tests have been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:201
msgid ""
"A CPP macro USE_THE_REPOSITORY_VARIABLE is introduced to help transition the "
"codebase to rely less on the availability of the singleton the_repository "
"instance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:204
msgid ""
"\"git version --build-options\" reports the version information of OpenSSL "
"and other libraries (if used) in the build."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:208
msgid ""
"Memory ownership rules for the in-core representation of remote.*.url "
"configuration values have been straightened out, which resulted in a few "
"leak fixes and code clarification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:212
msgid ""
"When bundleURI interface fetches multiple bundles, Git failed to take full "
"advantage of all bundles and ended up slurping duplicated objects, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:215
msgid ""
"The code to deal with modified paths that are out-of-cone in a sparsely "
"checked out working tree has been optimized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:218
msgid ""
"An existing test of oidmap API has been rewritten with the unit-test "
"framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:221
msgid ""
"The \"ort\" merge backend saw one bugfix for a crash that happens when inner "
"merge gets killed, and assorted code clean-ups."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:225
msgid ""
"A new warning message is issued when a command has to expand a sparse index "
"to handle working tree cruft that are outside of the sparse checkout."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:228
msgid ""
"The test framework learned to take the test body not as a single string but "
"as a here-document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:231
msgid ""
"\"git push '' HEAD:there\" used to hit a BUG(); it has been corrected to die "
"with \"fatal: bad repository ''\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:234
msgid ""
"What happens when http.cookieFile gets the special value \"\" has been "
"clarified in the documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.45"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:242
msgid ""
"\"git rebase --signoff\" used to forget that it needs to add a sign-off to "
"the resulting commit when told to continue after a conflict stops its "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:246
msgid ""
"The procedure to build multi-pack-index got confused by the replace-refs "
"mechanism, which has been corrected by disabling the latter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:251
msgid ""
"The \"-k\" and \"--rfc\" options of \"format-patch\" will now error out when "
"used together, as one tells us not to add anything to the title of the "
"commit, and the other one tells us to add \"RFC\" in addition to \"PATCH\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:254
msgid ""
"\"git stash -S\" did not handle binary files correctly, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:258
msgid ""
"A scheduled \"git maintenance\" job is expected to work on all repositories "
"it knows about, but it stopped at the first one that errored out.  Now it "
"keeps going."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:262
msgid ""
"zsh can pretend to be a normal shell pretty well except for some glitches "
"that we tickle in some of our scripts. Work them around so that \"vimdiff\" "
"and our test suite works well enough with it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:266
msgid ""
"Command line completion support for zsh (in contrib/) has been updated to "
"stop exposing internal state to end-user shell interaction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:270
msgid ""
"Tests that try to corrupt in-repository files in chunked format did not work "
"well on macOS due to its broken \"mv\", which has been worked around."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:272
msgid "The maximum size of attribute files is enforced more consistently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:275
msgid ""
"Unbreak CI jobs so that we do not attempt to use Python 2 that has been "
"removed from the platform."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:280
msgid ""
"Git 2.43 started using the tree of HEAD as the source of attributes in a "
"bare repository, which has severe performance implications.  For now, revert "
"the change, without ripping out a more explicit support for the attr.tree "
"configuration variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:283
msgid ""
"The \"--exit-code\" option of \"git diff\" command learned to work with the "
"\"--ext-diff\" option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:287
msgid ""
"Windows CI running in GitHub Actions started complaining about the order of "
"arguments given to calloc(); the imported regex code uses the wrong order "
"almost consistently, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:292
msgid ""
"Expose \"name conflict\" error when a ref creation fails due to D/F conflict "
"in the ref namespace, to improve an error message given by \"git fetch\".  "
"(merge 9339fca23e it/refs-name-conflict later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:295
msgid ""
"The SubmittingPatches document now refers folks to manpages translation "
"project."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:298
msgid ""
"The documentation for \"git diff --name-only\" has been clarified that it is "
"about showing the names in the post-image tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:303
msgid ""
"The credential helper that talks with osx keychain learned to avoid storing "
"back the authentication material it just got received from the keychain.  "
"(merge e1ab45b2da kn/osxkeychain-skip-idempotent-store later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:307
msgid ""
"The chainlint script (invoked during \"make test\") did nothing when it "
"failed to detect the number of available CPUs.  It now falls back to 1 CPU "
"to avoid the problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:311
msgid ""
"Revert overly aggressive \"layered defence\" that went into 2.45.1 and "
"friends, which broke \"git-lfs\", \"git-annex\", and other use cases, so "
"that we can rebuild necessary counterparts in the open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:315
msgid ""
"\"git init\" in an already created directory, when the user configuration "
"has includeif.onbranch, started to fail recently, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:317
msgid "Memory leaks in \"git mv\" has been plugged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:320
msgid ""
"The safe.directory configuration knob has been updated to optionally allow "
"leading path matches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:322
msgid "An overly large \".gitignore\" files are now rejected silently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:326
msgid ""
"Upon expiration event, the credential subsystem forgot to clear in-core "
"authentication material other than password (whose support was added "
"recently), which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:329
msgid ""
"Fix for an embarrassing typo that prevented Python2 tests from running "
"anywhere."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:332
msgid ""
"Varargs functions that are unannotated as printf-like or execl-like have "
"been annotated as such."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:339
msgid ""
"\"git am\" has a safety feature to prevent it from starting a new session "
"when there already is a session going.  It reliably triggers when a mbox is "
"given on the command line, but it has to rely on the tty-ness of the "
"standard input.  Add an explicit way to opt out of this safety with a "
"command line option.  (merge 62c71ace44 jk/am-retry later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:342
msgid "A leak in \"git imap-send\" that somehow escapes LSan has been plugged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:346
msgid ""
"Setting core.abbrev too early before the repository set-up (typically in "
"\"git clone\") caused segfault, which as been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:350
msgid ""
"When the user adds to \"git rebase -i\" instruction to \"pick\" a merge "
"commit, the error experience is not pleasant.  Such an error is now caught "
"earlier in the process that parses the todo list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:355
msgid ""
"We forgot to normalize the result of getcwd() to NFC on macOS where all "
"other paths are normalized, which has been corrected.  This still does not "
"address the case where core.precomposeUnicode configuration is not defined "
"globally."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:359
msgid ""
"Earlier we stopped using the tree of HEAD as the default source of "
"attributes in a bare repository, but failed to document it.  This has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:363
msgid ""
"\"git update-server-info\" and \"git commit-graph --write\" have been "
"updated to use the tempfile API to avoid leaving cruft after failing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:366
msgid ""
"An unused extern declaration for mingw has been removed to prevent it from "
"causing build failure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:369
msgid ""
"A helper function shared between two tests had a copy-paste bug, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:372
msgid ""
"\"git fetch-pack -k -k\" without passing \"--lock-pack\" (which we never do "
"ourselves) did not work at all, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:377
msgid ""
"CI job to build minimum fuzzers learned to pass NO_CURL=NoThanks to the "
"build procedure, as its build environment does not offer, or the rest of the "
"build needs, anything cURL.  (merge 4e66b5a990 jc/fuzz-sans-curl later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:381
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-ext-diff\" when diff.external is configured ignored the "
"\"--color-moved\" option.  (merge 0f4b0d4cf0 "
"rs/diff-color-moved-w-no-ext-diff-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:386
msgid ""
"\"git archive --add-virtual-file=<path>:<contents>\" never paid attention to "
"the --prefix=<prefix> option but the documentation said it would. The "
"documentation has been corrected.  (merge 72c282098d "
"jc/archive-prefix-with-add-virtual-file later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.46.0.txt:392
msgid ""
"When GIT_PAGER failed to spawn, depending on the code path taken, we failed "
"immediately (correct) or just spew the payload to the standard output "
"(incorrect).  The code now always fail immediately when GIT_PAGER fails.  "
"(merge 78f0a5d187 rj/pager-die-upon-exec-failure later to maint)."
msgstr ""

